   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Keystroke\n\nPhysical keycaps rise and press to show keyboard shortcuts, one chord after another.\n\nCategory: effects. Length: 6 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A product tutorial or demo needs to show which keyboard shortcut is being used.\n- Keys should feel physical, rising and pressing, rather than appear as flat text.\n\nAvoid when:\n- You need a flat caption: use a lower-third or text block.\n- The video has no keyboard action to illustrate.\n\nVariables:\n- steps (string): Steps, default \"[{\\\"at\\\":20,\\\"keys\\\":\\\"mod+k\\\"},{\\\"at\\\":78,\\\"keys\\\":\\\"g i\\\"},{\\\"at\\\":114,\\\"keys\\\":\\\"shift+mod+p\\\"}]\"\n- platform (enum): Platform, default \"mac\"\n- theme (enum): Theme, default \"light\"\n- accent (color): Accent, default \"#0a84ff\"\n- size (number, 32-128): Key size, default 64\n- linger (number, 0-90): Linger, default 30\n- x (number, 0-1): Center X, default 0.5\n- y (number, 0-1): Center Y, default 0.86\n- speed (number, 0.25-3): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
